1
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:06,159
couple of minutes every animal was at his post.

2
00:00:06,159 --> 00:00:12,199
As the human beings approached the farm buildings, Snowball launched his first attack.

3
00:00:12,199 --> 00:00:18,480
All the pigeons, to the number of 35, flew to and fro over the men's heads and

4
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:21,119
muted upon them from midair.

5
00:00:21,119 --> 00:00:25,199
And while the men were dealing with this, the geese, who had been hiding

6
00:00:25,199 --> 00:00:31,840
behind the hedge, rushed out and pecked viciously at the calves of their legs.

7
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:36,440
However, this was only a light skirmishing maneuver intended to create

8
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:42,360
a little disorder, and the men easily drove the geese off with their sticks.

9
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:46,559
Snowball now launched his second line of attack.

10
00:00:46,559 --> 00:00:51,960
Muriel, Benjamin, and all the sheep, with Snowball at the head of them,

11
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:58,320
rushed forward and prodded and butted the men from every side, while Benjamin

12
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:02,880
turned round and lashed at them with his small hoofs.

13
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:09,800
But once again, the men, with their sticks and their hobnailed boots, were too strong for them.

14
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:15,519
And suddenly, at a squeal from Snowball, which was the signal for retreat, all

15
00:01:15,519 --> 00:01:20,480
the animals turned and fled through the gateway into the yard.

16
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:23,840
The men gave a shout of triumph.

17
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:31,199
They saw, as they imagined, their enemies in flight, and they rushed after them in disorder.

18
00:01:31,199 --> 00:01:34,760
This was just what Snowball had intended.

19
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:39,239
As soon as they were well inside the yard, the three horses, the three cows,

20
00:01:39,239 --> 00:01:43,880
and the rest of the pigs, who had been lying in ambush in the cowshed, suddenly

21
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:47,519
emerged in their rear, cutting them off.

22
00:01:47,519 --> 00:01:51,760
Snowball now gave the signal for the charge.

23
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:55,599
He himself dashed straight for Jones.

24
00:01:55,599 --> 00:02:01,280
Jones saw him coming, raised his gun, and fired.

25
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:08,559
The pellets scored bloody streaks along Snowball's back, and a sheep dropped dead.

26
00:02:08,559 --> 00:02:16,000
Without halting for an instant, Snowball flung his 15 stone against Jones's legs.

27
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,239
Jones was hurled into a pile of dung, and his gun flew out of his hands.

28
00:02:22,239 --> 00:02:29,119
But the most terrifying spectacle of all was Boxer, rearing up on his hind legs

29
00:02:29,119 --> 00:02:35,280
and striking out with his great iron-shod hoofs like a stallion.

30
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:41,000
His very first blow took a stable-lad from Foxwood on the skull and stretched

31
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,519
him lifeless in the mud.

32
00:02:43,519 --> 00:02:49,119
At the sight, several men dropped their sticks and tried to run.

33
00:02:49,119 --> 00:02:54,559
Panic overtook them, and the next moment all the animals together were chasing

34
00:02:54,559 --> 00:02:58,039
them round and round the yard.

35
00:02:58,039 --> 00:03:03,360
They were gored, kicked, bitten, trampled on.

36
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:08,599
There was not an animal on the farm that did not take vengeance on them after his

37
00:03:08,599 --> 00:03:10,400
own fashion.

38
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:15,480
Even the cat suddenly leaped off a roof onto a carman's shoulders and sank her

39
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:20,400
claws in his neck, at which he yelled horribly.

40
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:25,000
At a moment when the opening was clear, the men were glad enough to rush out of

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,599
the yard and make a bolt for the main road.

42
00:03:28,599 --> 00:03:33,679
And so, within 5 minutes of their invasion, they were in ignominious

43
00:03:33,679 --> 00:03:38,000
retreat by the same way as they had come, with a flock of geese hissing after them
